Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 07:09:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Add opt-in DSH OpenCode Zen bridge

ONCODE_ZEN=1 now installs the DHS-M/dsh-opencode-zen integration alongside the
product patch:
- copies the standalone @deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-opencode adapter and the anonymous
  Exa MCP web-search plugin into the harness workspace
- registers both in the base/web-app bundle manifests and the host TS project
- points the default agent model at opencode-zen / big-pickle through the local
  shim route
- documents the opt-in flag in README and docs

The OpenCode Zen adapter must use named exports only; its upstream source
currently ends with 'export default apply', which makes the DSH Cordis loader
ignore inject/name metadata. install.sh removes that default export when
adapting the package.
