+### Opt-in OpenCode Zen bridge
+
+Pass `OPENCODE_ZEN=1` to also add the [DSH OpenCode Zen bridge](https://github.com/DHS-M/dsh-opencode-zen) from the same organization. It installs the standalone `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-opencode` adapter, the anonymous Exa MCP web-search plugin, and points the default agent model at `opencode-zen` / `big-pickle` through a local loopback route.
+
+```bash
+OPENCODE_ZEN=1 BUILD=1 ./install.sh "$HOME/dsh-remote-web"
+```
+
+Start the Zen shim (or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) before using the route:
+
+```bash
+node <dsh-opencode-zen>/zen_shim.js
+```
+
+If you are not calling the real OpenCode Zen endpoint, the bridge still works against an OpenAI-compatible `/v1` server bound to `http://127.0.0.1:8791`.
+
 ## Run the web interface
 
 ```bash
